  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nA batch with five separate centered dyadic BIT outputs normally restores each output's address layout independently. Allowing the common source to be temporarily permuted lets those outputs share one query tour: **40 to 13 complete ordinary ADDRESS children**, **240 to 78 affine events**, and the same **30 XOR scans**, with no extra full row. The comparison already uses PR953's optimized separate-target batches.\n\nThis is a **scoped recursive-interface construction; no new kappa**. Every output, source and dirty spectator has the correct endpoint. The changed permission is essential: the source must be exclusively writable and unobserved until batch exit. Thirteen queries are proved minimal only in the declared source-query/output-XOR alphabet. Each query has its full seven-event lowering and complete coefficient-specific invoice; the new query histogram is componentwise dominated by the baseline.\n\nThe [proof and typed recurrence](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/README.md) retain role-dependent child/affine prices and all preparation, source access, routing, dispatch, temporary storage and restoration costs. No physical supplier caller, DATA-to-ADDRESS recursive compiler, all-size/tape/hosting admission, runtime saving or analytic transfer is established. The selected record is unchanged.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nBase: `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`. Contribution: `04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2`. OS assignment seed **55**, recursive interfaces; **refined** `persistent-boundary` scope. [Task card](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/TASK.json) \u00b7 [source pins](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/SOURCES.json) \u00b7 [claim #1493](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1493).\n\nThe new object has distinct output ports and a temporarily mutable shared source. PR953 at `5f052969846b0882ac4e22d9e818dd8ac05ea56f` batches several terms on one target with an unchanged source; PR840 at `da2cd0dd2229e08b61b174a8835a2c2bb99d2230` provides the signed dyadic lowering and pair construction. Their results are credited and reused. PR1235 is related source-tour reasoning in a different phase/rank model.\n\nThe [final overlap snapshot](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/OVERLAP.json) covers **759 open PRs and 193 discussion/comment records**, complete pagination and no warnings. Nearby Discussions1501 and1505 explicitly distinguish their additive-connector and port-borrowing scopes. This is bounded overlap evidence, not a novelty certificate. Only this new research directory is added.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/shared-dyadic-source\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_SHARED_DYADIC_SOURCE children=40->13 affine=240->78 XOR=30 patterns=768 no_new_kappa`, seven passing package tests, then `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`.\n\n- All **768** declared small incidence patterns; separate Laurent and cyclic dirty-state/inverse checks; **25,088** cyclic dirty columns per implementation.\n- All thirteen native powers: **104** rational columns, **624** modular columns and **850,408** complete six-field ADDRESS/spectator inputs. Both complete array words pass **20,412** dirty columns per implementation.\n- **24** mathematical/admission controls, including every native event omission and a collapsed-output word whose aggregate is correct while the separate outputs are wrong.\n- Python **3.12.2** registered replay, seven package tests and all **20** onboarding tests pass on macOS arm64. Optimized isolated Python **3.14.6** source export without Git reproduces the exact receipt byte-for-byte, keeps read-only files unchanged, and rejects an actual corrupted evidence file. Source/certificate corruption and missing-child controls pass.\n- `make selected-record-check`, source-pin metadata and staged whitespace checks pass. Refreshed main and all ten inputs remain identical. [Validation record](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/VALIDATION.json).\n\nFinite tests support the separate written proof; they are not formal verification of the multiplication theorem. Selected cold replay, physical tape/compiler execution, hosted CI acceptance and independent human review were not performed.\n\n## Credit\n\nHanson Sun (@bbMisk), with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in derivation, implementation, checks and prose; Apache-2.0. Credit Ross Richardson/PR953, Wentao Li/PR840, Karl Appel/PR521, commdata2338/PR677, their retained eumemic/Ali Romman lineage, Richard Hoekstra/PR1235, and OpenAI's framework maintained by Douglas Colkitt. Original notices and licenses are source-pinned inputs. No priority is claimed for the native lowering, single-target tour or generic source-gauge idea.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n[The package](https://github.com/bbMisk/integer-mult-bounds/blob/04379bb9bf8d394891df9b48edbfa79882aedae2/research/shared-dyadic-source/README.md#open-next-questions) gives two bounded follow-ups: find an actual caller with no intermediate source observation and price its complete supplier invoice; or study a small formal Laurent instance permitting queries on both source and outputs. A concrete caller/compiler is the blocker to adoption, and the current complex supplier remains binding.\n",
